    "pdpPlainTextPreview": "The design is by Dominique Evans, the designer of the Jane Austen 2017 UK Coin\nWE ARE STRENGTHENING ACCOUNT SECURITY AND PROTECTING YOUR ACCESS WITH 2 STEP VERIFICATION. FIND OUT MORE Home Shop Monarch Elizabeth II 2020 Celebrating British Diversity 50p Silver Proof Share via Silver Proof 2020 Celebrating British Diversity 50p Silver Proof Limited Edition 25,000 Price: £55.00 EMAIL ME WHEN IN STOCK Email Me When In Stock PRODUCT CODE: HISDU50 This is the first UK coin to celebrate diversity, and mark the contribution of ethnic minorities in building a modern, prosperous Britain The design is by Dominique Evans, the designer of the Jane Austen 2017 UK Coin Struck in sterling silver and finished to Proof standard The coin is unique in seeking to embrace all elements of diversity in Britain Silver Proof Read the full description YOU MIGHT ALSO BE INTERESTED IN ADD TO BASKET Britannia 2026 1oz Silver Bullion Coin £62.47 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Britannia 2022 1 oz Silver Bullion Coin £61.27 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Level 5 Genius Medal £9.95 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Britannia 2026 1oz Gold Bullion Coin £3,484.37 In Stock ADD TO BASKET 100th Anniversary of the Birth of Queen Elizabeth II 2026 UK £5 Brilliant Uncirculated Coin £17.50 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Britannia 2026 1oz Silver Bullion Twenty-Five Coin Tube £1,481.75 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Level 4 Mastermind Medal £9.95 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Britannia 1g Gold Bullion Minted Bar £140.68 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Level 3 Decoder Medal £9.95 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Level 2 Explorer Medal and Collector Folder £9.95 In Stock Dominique Evans, Designer at The Royal Mint, said: “When designing this coin, I began by thinking about the people who inspire me and what diversity has meant in my life. I believe that no matter where you are born, we all belong under the same sky and this was the starting point of the design. “The background of the coin features a geodome with a series of interconnecting lines and triangles that form a network. Each part is equal, and symbolises a community of connection and strength. The words ‘DIVERSITY BUILT BRITAIN’ talks about the differences between us, and the connection which gives us unity. The design also looks to the future, how we can connect, develop bonds and grow stronger together.” Anne Jessopp, CEO of The Royal Mint, said: “Britain’s history is rich and diverse. For more than 1,100 years, the nation’s story has been told through coins struck by The Royal Mint, a narrative carried in the pockets and purses of all its people. The contribution of ethnic minority communities has been such an important part of that story but has often gone unrecognised. This coin has been created to celebrate all the people who have made Britain what it is today. This is a very exciting development for us and the launch of this important coin coincides with Black History Month, signalling a change in UK coinage, one that I am personally delighted to pioneer.” SPECIFICATION Specification Value Alloy .925 Sterling Silver Weight 8.00 g Diameter 27.30mm Reverse Designer Dominique Evans Obverse Designer Jody Clark Specification Value Quality Proof Year 2020 Pure Metal Type Silver"
